            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic, antipyretic and anti-inflammatory effects of essential oil of Lippia multiflora.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The essential oil of Lippia multiflora Moldenke (Verbenaceae) produced by conventional hydrodistillation was analyzed and studied for its analgesic, antipyretic and anti-inflammatory activities in rats and mice. At the doses used (2, 4 and 8 ml/kg o.s.) the essential oil of L. multiflora showed significant and dose-dependent analgesic effect on acetic acid-induced writhing in mice. Only the dose of 8 ml/kg of essential oil, antagonized hyperexia induced by brewer's yeast. No effect on granuloma formation was observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
